# Replace every example URL with an operator-controlled HTTPS endpoint.
# Keep this file non-secret; configure values in the deployment secret manager.
FACTORY_META_DATABASE=/data/meta-connector.sqlite
FACTORY_META_OIDC_ISSUER=https://identity.example.com/
FACTORY_META_OIDC_AUDIENCE=code-factory-meta-connector
FACTORY_META_JWKS_URL=https://identity.example.com/.well-known/jwks.json
FACTORY_META_AUTHORIZATION_URL=https://identity.example.com/oauth/authorize
FACTORY_META_TOKEN_URL=https://identity.example.com/oauth/token

# OAuth provider configuration, not application environment variables:
# - Authorization code with PKCE S256; use Meta's assigned redirect URI.
# - Publish scopes cf.audit.read, cf.audit.write, cf.audit.link.
# - Issue RS256 JWT access tokens with iss, aud, sub, tenant_id, jti,
#   groups (array of strings), scope, iat, exp; maximum lifetime 900 seconds.
# - Include auth_time on fresh relink grants. Configure refresh-token rotation
#   and revocation at the provider. Never put OAuth client secrets here.
# - Restrict Meta-exposed tools to cf.audit.read endpoints in onboarding.
